# 7. Verify Home Directory and Login Shell Configuration

The account database can be inspected with:

```bash
getent passwd <username>
```

or:

```bash
cat /etc/passwd
```

A passwd entry contains fields including:

```text
username:x:UID:GID:comment:home:shell
```

For example:

```text
alice:x:1002:1005::/home/alice:/bin/bash
```

This verifies that the account configuration points to:

```text
Home:  /home/alice
Shell: /bin/bash
```

To verify that the directory itself physically exists, also use:

```bash
ls -ld /home/alice
```

This distinction matters:

```text
/etc/passwd
     │
     └── says where the home directory SHOULD be

ls -ld /home/alice
     │
     └── proves the directory actually EXISTS
```

