# 18. Incident Encountered During Lab

## INC-1002A — Developers Cannot Create Application Files

### Symptoms

Developers could access an existing test file but could not create another file under:

```text
/srv/webapp
```

Alice was confirmed to belong to:

```text
developers
```

The directory was inspected:

```bash
ls -ld /srv/webapp
```

Result:

```text
drwxr-sr-x root developers /srv/webapp
```

Alice's membership was inspected:

```bash
id alice
```

Result showed:

```text
alice → developers
```

---

# 19. Root Cause Analysis

Break down the directory permissions:

```text
d | rwx | r-s | r-x
    │      │     │
    │      │     └── other
    │      └──────── group: developers
    └─────────────── owner: root
```

The group had:

```text
r-s
```

The missing permission was:

```text
w
```

Therefore:

```text
Alice
  │
  ├── authenticated ................ YES
  ├── developers member ............ YES
  ├── can access directory ......... YES
  ├── can read existing resources .. YES
  │
  └── can create directory entry ... NO
                                      │
                                      ▼
                              Permission denied
```

The directory itself lacked group write permission.

---

# 20. Resolution

Group write permission was granted to the shared application directory.

After remediation, the effective design became:

```text
                   /srv/webapp
                        │
                root:developers
                        │
                  group = rwx
                  setgid = ON
                        │
             ┌──────────┴──────────┐
             │                     │
           alice                  bob
        developers             developers
             │                     │
             ├── create ───────────┤
             │                     │
             └──── shared files ───┘
```

---

# 21. Verification

The fix was not considered complete merely because `ls` showed the expected permissions.

Functional testing was performed.

### Alice

Switched to Alice's account:

```bash
su - alice
```

Alice successfully created another file under `/srv/webapp`.

### Bob

Switched to Bob's account:

```bash
su - bob
```

Bob successfully edited and saved the file Alice created.

This proved **cross-developer collaboration**, not merely directory visibility.

